<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/SUNA_V2/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/SUNA_V2/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/SUNA_V2/>;
    dc:modified '2021-08-19T11:48:30'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'SUNA_V2'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Submersible Ultraviolet Nitrate Analyser (SUNA) V2 nitrate sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A sensor using ultraviolet absorption spectroscopy to measure in-situ nitrate (NO3) concentration in real time and over clear to high turbidity/suspended sedimentation waters, depth-rated to 500 m. A deuterium lamp provides a light source of 10 mm path length (or 5 mm for high turbidity conditions); the measured spectrum falls within the Ultraviolet (UV) 190 nm - 370 nm wavelength range. The instrument is based on the MBARI-ISUS technology; it was originally developed and manufactured at Satlantic, and was rebranded as a Sea-Bird Scientific product following the company\'s acquisition by Danaher in 2011.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:R27::SUNA_V2'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/SUNA/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/SUNA/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/SUNA/>;
    dc:modified '2021-08-19T11:47:24'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'SUNA'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Submersible Ultraviolet Nitrate Analyser (SUNA) nitrate sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A sensor using ultraviolet absorption spectroscopy to measure in-situ nitrate (NO3) concentration in real time and over a variety of environments, depth-rated to 100 m. A deuterium lamp provides a light source of 1 cm path length; the measured spectrum falls within the Ultraviolet (UV) 190 nm - 370 nm wavelength range. Measurement accuracy: +/- 2 umol/l or 10 %; detection range: 0.5 umol/l to 2000 umol/l. The instrument is based on the MBARI-ISUS technology; it was originally developed and manufactured at Satlantic, and was rebranded as a Sea-Bird Scientific product following the company\'s acquisition by Danaher in 2011.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:R27::SUNA'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/SEASCAN_SSTD/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/SEASCAN_SSTD/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/SEASCAN_SSTD/>;
    dc:modified '2021-08-19T11:24:56'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'SEASCAN_SSTD'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Seascan Temperature and Depth (SSTD) sensor package'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A temperature and pressure sensor package developed by Seascan, composed of a high-stability, glass-encapsulated thermistor manufactured by YSI (or optionally an ultra-stable thermistor manufactured by Thermometrics), and a mono-crystal silicon strain gage sensor manufactured by Druck. YSI thermistor accuracy: 0.01 degC; YSI thermistor resolution: 0.001 degC; pressure transducer accuracy: 0.1 % of full scale. Instrument\'s depth rating: either 2000 dbar or 4000 dbar.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:R27::SEASCAN_SSTD'^^xsd:string .
